  "contentPlaintext": "<bold>Product Roadmap</bold>\nThis document outlines our strategic delivery timeline, feature milestones, and engineering focus areas across the next three execution horizons. It aligns product development cycles directly with our core business objectives.\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Strategic Themes & Execution Horizons\n2.1 Core Investment Themes\n2.2 Delivery Horizons Matrix\n3. Detailed Milestone Chronology\n3.1 Horizon 1: Now (Sprints 12 - 15)\n3.2 Horizon 2: Next (Sprints 16 - 19)\n3.3 Horizon 3: Later (Sprints 20+)\n4. Dependencies, Capacity & Resource Allocation\n4.1 Engineering Resource Split\n4.2 Critical Cross-Team Dependencies\n<bold>2. Strategic Themes & Execution Horizons</bold>\n<bold>2.1 Core Investment Themes</bold>\nOur product strategy focuses on three core pillars to keep the platform reliable, performant, and competitive:\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Infrastructure Reliability & Latency Reduction:</textStyle></bold> Optimizing system processing loops to keep P95 response times below 200ms.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Self-Service Data Integration:</textStyle></bold> Automating data ingestion tasks to minimize onboarding blockages for clients.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Enterprise Security Guardrails:</textStyle></bold> Deploying strict identity isolation frameworks and multi-factor authentication tools.\n<bold>2.2 Delivery Horizons Matrix</bold>\n[ Horizon 1: NOW ]  ─────────►  [ Horizon 2: NEXT ]  ─────────►  [ Horizon 3: LATER ]\n  Sprints 12 - 15                 Sprints 16 - 19                 Sprints 20+\n  (Active Execution)              (Grooming & Design)             (Strategic Backlog)\n<bold>3. Detailed Milestone Chronology</bold>\n<bold>3.1 Horizon 1: Now (Sprints 12 - 15)</bold>\nThis horizon focuses on shipping our core data ingestion and identity verification modules.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Epic: Batch Data Ingestion Core (</textStyle></bold><code>BDI</code><bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">)</textStyle></bold>\n<italic>Deliverables:</italic> Asynchronous ring-buffered queues, schema validation tables, and local file storage adapters.\n<italic>Target Version:</italic> v1.1.0-Beta\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Epic: Identity Isolation Engine (</textStyle></bold><code>UMA</code><bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">)</textStyle></bold>\n<italic>Deliverables:</italic> JWT token validation handlers, multi-factor login checks, and automated access lockout rules.\n<italic>Target Version:</italic> v1.1.0-Beta\n<bold>3.2 Horizon 2: Next (Sprints 16 - 19)</bold>\nThis horizon centers on building real-time telemetry visibility and expanding API automation.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Epic: Real-Time Analytics Dashboard (</textStyle></bold><code>RTE</code><bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">)</textStyle></bold>\n<italic>Deliverables:</italic> Responsive tabular data displays, layout caching layers, and secure PDF/CSV report generation.\n<italic>Target Version:</italic> v1.2.0-GA\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Epic: Automated Webhook Dispatcher (</textStyle></bold><code>AWD</code><bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">)</textStyle></bold>\n<italic>Deliverables:</italic> Outbound transaction notification triggers, payload retry loops, and event monitoring logs.\n<italic>Target Version:</italic> v1.2.0-GA\n<bold>3.3 Horizon 3: Later (Sprints 20+)</bold>\nLong-term exploratory efforts designed to optimize global scaling and data safety.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Epic: Distributed Edge Ingestion Network</textStyle></bold>\n<italic>Focus:</italic> Multi-region caching configurations to minimize packet transit latency for remote clients.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Epic: ML-Driven Anomaly Detection Gateway</textStyle></bold>\n<italic>Focus:</italic> Lightweight pattern check layers to intercept malicious transaction vectors before parsing runs.\n<bold>4. Dependencies, Capacity & Resource Allocation</bold>\n<bold>4.1 Engineering Resource Split</bold>\nTo safeguard stability while delivering features, our capacity allocation follows a strict resource split:\n[ Features: 50% ] ───&gt; [ Tech Debt/Maintenance: 30% ] ───&gt; [ Research/Spikes: 20% ]\n<bold>4.2 Critical Cross-Team Dependencies</bold>\nDependency ID\nTarget Epic Component\nImpacting Team\nResolution Action Plan\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">DEP-01</textStyle></bold>\nMulti-factor Login (<code>UMA</code>)\nSecurity / Infrastructure\nProvision staging identity tokens before Sprint 14 to prevent deployment pauses.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">DEP-02</textStyle></bold>\nAnalytics Dashboard (<code>RTE</code>)\nUI / UX Design Team\nFinalize visual component design systems and data grid frames by Sprint 15.",
